      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I understand the test. It verifies that `CodecEncoding.getCodec` throws an `IOException` when given a Run codec value (137, which falls in range 117-140) and a disconnected `PipedInputStream` that fails when read. Let me write the improved version.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored test adds a descriptive method name and explanatory comments clarifying why value 137 triggers the Run codec branch and why an unconnected `PipedInputStream` causes the expected `IOException`."
